{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c387","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4fd-996a-7423-ba27-e5daf29de5a2"},"sequence":30,"recorded_at":1780531400000055,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c4fe-a662-7da2-9ec1-3f56d452c904"},"task_id":"01a0c4fe-a662-7da2-9ec1-3f56d452c904","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c4fe-a662-7da2-9ec1-3f56d452c904","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-1-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-35urbp, status=development)' 2>&1; echo \\\"---\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_producer.md 2>&1 | head -200\",\n  \"description\": \"Set status and read producer brief\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"status_changed\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-35urbp\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-dev\\\"},\\\"side_effects\\\":[{\\\"action\\\":\\\"escalated\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"STORY-260830-2t4g7i\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-dev\\\"},{\\\"action\\\":\\\"escalated\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"EPIC-260830-1uwj54\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"reviewing\\\"}]}}\\n---\\nImplement TASK-260830-35urbp (implement-private-tmux-server-management), the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend). The chain is 35urbp -> TASK-260830-1c28dz (tmux lifecycle operations) -> TASK-260830-g0pcnt (generation and attach semantics, the final leaf). You own only this leaf.\\n\\nAUTHORITY. The task record's Scope names the spec at v0.5.0. That reference is STALE: this repository adopted v0.7.0 (STORY-260917-110onn, landed) and the pinned copy is `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`. Your normative authority is its **§4.2 tmux backend** (lines 1403-1449), with **§4.C Lifecycle and operations** (1082), **§4.D Closed capabilities and evidence** (1220) and **§4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility** (1309) as its context. Quote the pinned file, never the network, and never a v0.5.0 line number.\\n\\nWHAT THIS LEAF MUST DELIVER. Owner-only runtime directories and dedicated `tmux -S` server management, provably without ambient or default-server discovery or reuse. The normative rules you are implementing, in the spec's own words:\\n1. AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server and MUST NOT discover or reuse the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. \\\"By ambient socket name\\\" is the measurable part: an environment variable, an inherited socket, a default path and a conventional name are four separate vectors and each needs its own refusal row.\\n2. On macOS, server creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server.\\n3. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon, or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation. The fall-back prohibition is the rule most likely to be implemented as a comment rather than as a gate — a reviewer will plant a direct-creation call on the background path and expect a committed test to redden.\\n4. `launchctl managername` is a diagnostic hint ONLY. A cached sentinel or a prior `managername` observation MUST NOT authorize anything. If you expose any readiness fact, make its non-authorizing character a driven test, not a sentence.\\n5. Runtime directories are owner-only. Treat the mode, the ownership and the containment of that directory as three separate gates, and remember the landed lesson that lexical containment plus `O_NOFOLLOW` is NOT containment: check `internal/secprim` and the openat-relative walk that already exists before writing any path logic of your own.\\n\\nDETERMINISM IS A HARD CONSTRAINT, AND IT SHAPES THE DESIGN. AGENTS.md requires tests that are deterministic and free of network or terminal dependencies. tmux 3.6a happens to be installed on this host; that is NOT a licence to depend on it. Requirement: every rule above must be driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with no tmux process anywhere. If you also write a test that talks to a real tmux server, it must be separately gated and it must NOT be the only witness for any acceptance row — state in the results which rows, if any, have a real-tmux witness in addition to their deterministic one. How you achieve that is your design decision; do not ask, and do not degrade a rule into a mock-only shape to make it testable. If a rule genuinely cannot be driven without a live server, say so as an explicit BOUND with the reason, rather than pretending.\\n\\nDO NOT FORK A LANDED OWNER. This repository already carries `internal/terminalbackend` (18.6k lines), `internal/axpane` (8.8k), `internal/terminstance` (7.1k) and `internal/termbind` (4.5k), plus `internal/secprim`/`internal/secconftest` for path and argv safety, `internal/environ` for environment handling, `internal/canonicaljson` and `internal/scalar` for closed shapes and the AX number model. Read them BEFORE you write a type. Your predecessor dependency TASK-260830-2056mm landed in STORY-260830-ptxkqe (PR #55) — read `TASK-260830-2056mm_results.md` and its accepted verdict, because the pane/terminal-instance binding it delivered is what your server management has to sit under. Say in the results which existing type or gate you extended and which you deliberately did not. Every fork this epic produced became a defect.\\n\\nTRACEABILITY. Do NOT edit `internal/traceability` (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf (g0pcnt) carries the registry bindings and the re-pin. Document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and in the conformance matrix instead.\\n\\nEVIDENCE CONTRACT (repository DoD). Every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; a negative for every refusal, asserting the literal spec token (`capability_unavailable`) and the typed realm/readiness detail, not a production constant; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__` anywhere); crash and idempotency evidence for every durable write — creating a runtime directory and a server socket IS a durable write, so the landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern applies, or state an explicit purity bound; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; a README package section with test commands and NO capability or CLI claim (no `ax` command exists yet); a LOGBOOK entry, newest-first.\\n\\nWORKSPACE. This is the FIRST leaf, so the managed Story worktree does not exist yet — the spawn provisions `.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree` on branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i` forked from trunk `799c338`. Your candidate is the UNCOMMITTED working tree there: exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. If origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-35urbp`, then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that also appears in your `git status` and restore trunk content by hand — a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies of trunk-changed files into the candidate and they read as reverts. Before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths.\\n\\nPROCESS. Read the Curator-managed `go-testing-tools` skill first. All CI is local; never trigger hosted CI. Run your own package tests and the harness BEFORE handoff, then the full configured validation suite once — read the command count from the candidate's `task-board.config.json` (it is 30 at trunk 799c338, not 27); command 5 is `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs, which is expected and must not be shortened. Report the coverage ratio you MEASURED. Hand off no later than 3.5 hours in; if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-35urbp_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-35urbp --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.\\nREJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\\n(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\\n(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\\n(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\\n(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\\n(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\\n(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \\\"Composes X\\\", \\\"never admits what decoding refuses\\\", \\\"nothing re-implemented\\\", \\\"no cached sentinel can authorize\\\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\\nFinally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 11382,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2846,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
