{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3b9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4fd-996a-7423-ba27-e5daf29de5a2"},"sequence":55,"recorded_at":1780531400000105,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c4fe-bd35-7b90-adb5-d7f73246a13f"},"task_id":"01a0c4fe-bd35-7b90-adb5-d7f73246a13f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c4fe-bd35-7b90-adb5-d7f73246a13f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-2-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev6.md 2>&1 | head -300\\necho \\\"=====REVIEWER CR5=====\\\"\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_reviewer-cr5.md 2>&1 | head -200\",\n  \"description\": \"Read latest rework and reviewer briefs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev5.md and every earlier precondition. Do exactly what is written here.\\nRework run for TASK-260830-35urbp, the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i. Revision 5 was reviewed by RUN-260921-60d15f (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED with **no P1**: one P2 (four measured members) and two P3. Read TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev5.md first. Every rev4 finding — the oracle fix and the admit-direction narrowing, `Request.Name`, the platform axis, the spy census, the five observation sentences — is closed with driven evidence and stays closed. **Production behaves correctly at every point five consecutive reviews have driven.** Keep all of it.\\nTrunk has NOT moved (base is still 799c338). Your working tree is the rev5 candidate; build revision 6 on it. Do not refresh, do not rebase.\\n\\n**READ THIS BEFORE THE ITEM LIST, BECAUSE IT IS THE ACTUAL TASK.** Three rounds in a row have produced the same class of finding at a new site each time: rev3 P2-C (the running-server rule pinned at the entry only for servers carrying admission data), rev4 P2-B (`Request.Name` free at the entry while the path was pinned at the constants), and now rev5 P2-A (the broker-or-refuse rule pinned at the entry only for the shapes the fixtures happen to build). Each round I handed you the specific tests the reviewer had already measured, you closed exactly those, and the next review found the same class one site over. **That means the defect is your measurement, not your code.** So this round the deliverable is the instrument, and the enumerated items below are only its first outputs.\\n\\nBuild and commit a **gate × entry census**. For every gate in the package, list every production entry that can reach it — `Acquire` foreground, `Acquire` background, the exported `EnsureRuntimeDir`, `VerifyRuntimeDir`, `BuildArgv`, `SocketPath`, `CheckBrokerContact`, `CheckServerAttested` and anything else that composes them. For every (gate, entry) cell, state one of exactly three things: a named committed test that drives the gate THROUGH that entry and an admitting narrowing row that it kills; or `unreachable` with the reason a caller cannot get there; or a stated BOUND naming what is not measured and who owns it. Put the census in the conformance matrix as its own table and mirror its shape in TRACEABILITY. A cell that says \\\"pinned at the helper\\\" and nothing else is exactly the hole the last three reviews walked through — a helper pin plus an entry that reaches the same gate is two cells, not one. Count the cells and report the ratio you MEASURE. If the census is honest and some cells are bounds, that is an acceptable revision; another round of four tests without the census is not.\\n\\nThe four members the reviewer already measured are your first four cells, and the probes named are templates:\\n1. **Broker-side attested-server wiring has no admitting narrowing.** SPEC §4.2 1419-1424 requires the background caller to contact an already-running authenticated broker **and its attested server**, else `capability_unavailable`, never a fallback. Four plants that each admit one realistic member SURVIVED both passes: the zero `RealmAdmission{}` report with a live same-user generation-bound principal (the nothing-reconciled state, the exact shape rev3 closed on the FOREGROUND path); rows present with an empty generation against a bound wanted generation; a decoy-only admission with a bound generation (the member the foreground entry already pins); and a background miss whose `Dependencies` carry the foreground `ProbeServer`, which re-enters foreground creation — realistic, because the lifecycle adapter will pass one shared `Dependencies` value to every caller, and no committed background test arms `ProbeServer`, so the `Spawn`-keyed spy census never sees it. Ship: three subtests on `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` asserting the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6, the five typed details and zero spawns; the same three rows mirrored on `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`; a narrowing row at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring named under rows 27/28/36; a fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy armed in every background miss test plus `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`, shipped as a second labelled additive row `D-background-fallback-foreground`; and the row-31/README sentence extended to say the census arms BOTH foreground dependencies.\\n2. **The absence classifier's reject class is pinned at the entry for mode and containment only.** Widening `runtimeAbsent` to admit `runtime ownership` SURVIVED both passes: no committed background `Acquire` test stages foreign ownership, so a foreign-owned leaf on the background path would return `capability_unavailable` with the custody error redacted as its cause — refusal-to-refusal, but row 52 says an unsafe leaf keeps its custody code as the TOP-LEVEL `*Error`, never the wrapper. Add `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (the `effectiveUID` seam is the lever) under row 52, or state the ownership member as helper-pinned only in the census.\\n3. **A censusable \\\"before\\\" that is false.** `acquire.go:140-143` and `results.md:61-62` both claim malformed input, ambient reuse and missing dependencies \\\"refuse before any side effect\\\". A foreground request with `SessionID = \\\"12345\\\"` **creates `<root>/tmux` and calls `ProbeServer` before** refusing `tmux_invalid_arguments at session identity`: the session identity is validated only inside `BuildArgv`, after `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe. Either parse the session at the `Acquire` entry before any side effect and add no-directory/no-probe assertions to `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` (row 45), or reword both sentences to the members that are actually true. Rejection pattern (f), and the third time a sentence with a universal quantifier has cost a round — before you write \\\"every\\\", \\\"all\\\", \\\"never\\\" or \\\"before any\\\", make the census cell that proves it.\\n4. **Three observation sentences for TRACEABILITY**, all cheap: a comma inside the runtime root makes `tmuxEnvSocket` split at the wrong comma so a real-encoding `TMUX` value walks past the collision gate — tmux(1) itself splits at the first comma, so the decoding is faithful and the honest text is \\\"roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX member's encoding\\\" in row 23/B16; a cwd-relative spelling of the derived socket walks past the cleaned-string collision gate, the same bound class as the symlink alias, so B16 should read \\\"symlinked or relative alias\\\"; and `Dependencies.Spawn` is inert on the background path.\\n\\nPROCESS. Keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED; exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept, and do NOT touch `internal/traceability` — the final leaf g0pcnt carries the registry. Run your own package tests, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` (keep it green), and the harness BEFORE handoff, then the full configured suite once, reading the commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` in the candidate config. A second Story is producing concurrently on this host, so command 5 will be slow; do NOT shorten it, and if a gate times out report the measured elapsed time and the host load rather than arguing it away. Update the results with a finding-by-finding table AND the gate × entry census with its measured ratio, update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, MANIFEST with no self-entry, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, zero `__pycache__`), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-35urbp --role developer` so revision 6 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 3 hours in. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 6.\\nREJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\\n(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\\n(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\\n(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\\n(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\\n(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\\n(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \\\"Composes X\\\", \\\"never admits what decoding refuses\\\", \\\"nothing re-implemented\\\", \\\"no cached sentinel can authorize\\\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\\nFinally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.\\n=====REVIEWER CR5=====\\nIndependently review Change Request revision 5 of TASK-260830-35urbp (implement-private-tmux-server-management), the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend; the chain is 35urbp -> 1c28dz -> g0pcnt). Change Request shape: task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base 799c338; checkpointed predecessors none; tip 799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2), published by RUN-260921-615903 on muse-spark max, 22 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-35urbp_change-request_rev5.patch / _rev5-validation.log. Revisions 1..4 are earlier construction attempts of the same producer scope that failed the Change Request validation suite on the pre-PR51 10m race-test timeout under concurrent suites; they carry no review verdict and no prior review findings — review revision 5 on its own merits.. Read the producer brief TASK-260830-35urbp_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes.\\n\\nNORMATIVE AUTHORITY: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` **§3.2** (lines 806-813, which fix the runtime root, the socket path `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` and its component-by-component custody) and **§4.2 tmux backend** (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220), §4.E (1309) and §4.4 (1478-1490) as context. §3.2 was missing from the producer's authority list for revisions 1-3 and the rev3 review found the candidate diverging from it, so check it explicitly: the derived path, the identity of `Request.Root` as the Runtime IPC root rather than the durable state root, and whether any committed test pins the old literals and therefore defends a divergence. The task record's Scope still names v0.5.0 and that is stale — if the candidate cites a v0.5.0 line number or quotes text that is not in the pinned file, that is a finding. Derive every expectation from the spec text, never from a production constant.\\n\\nVerify with your own instruments, on isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree; never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration.\\n\\n(1) **The dedicated-server rule, per vector.** \\\"AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server and MUST NOT discover or reuse the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name\\\" is not one gate. Drive each vector separately — an environment variable naming a socket, an inherited socket, a default path, a conventional name — and for each, assert the refusal at the production entry the matrix names. A candidate that closes one vector and reports the class is the single most likely shape here; census the call sites and plant a fresh spelling that walks through.\\n\\n(2) **The background-caller rules, which are the hard part.** A Background caller MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated broker and its attested server, and if neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation. Plant a direct-creation call on the background path and require a committed test to redden; a fall-back prohibition implemented as a comment, a doc line or an unreachable branch is a P1. Assert the LITERAL token `capability_unavailable` and the typed realm/readiness detail, not `== pkg.SomeConst` — swap the constant to another registered value with the same exit and see whether the suite notices.\\n\\n(3) **`launchctl managername` is a diagnostic hint only, and a cached sentinel or prior observation MUST NOT authorize.** This is exactly the shape that has been faked on this epic before with a reflection census of field names. Drive a cached/stale observation into the production entry and assert it authorizes nothing; a name census is not an effect census.\\n\\n(4) **Owner-only runtime directories.** Mode, ownership and containment are three gates. Check specifically that path logic delegates to the landed `internal/secprim` openat-relative walk rather than re-implementing containment: lexical containment plus `O_NOFOLLOW` is not containment, a symlinked intermediate escapes it, and a check after `open()` never runs on a FIFO. Plant a symlinked intermediate component and a FIFO.\\n\\n(5) **The determinism constraint, verified not read.** The brief required every rule to be driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere, with any real-tmux test separately gated and never the only witness for an acceptance row. Verify it by running the suite in an environment where tmux cannot be reached (make the binary unresolvable in your isolated copy) and reporting exactly which tests fail or skip. A row whose only witness skips in that run is an unmeasured row, however green the producer's log looks. Also check the converse: a rule degraded into a mock-only shape so it could be tested is a finding, not a solution — the production entry must still be the thing under test.\\n\\n(6) **No forked owners.** `internal/terminalbackend`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/secprim`, `internal/environ`, `internal/canonicaljson`, `internal/scalar` are landed. Grep for a second model of anything they already own (string bounds in characters not bytes, uint53 and the AX number model, digests, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, argv and path safety). The results must name which existing type or gate was extended; verify that claim rather than accepting it — \\\"composes X\\\" and \\\"nothing re-implemented\\\" are censusable claims.\\n\\n(7) **Traceability boundary.** This leaf must NOT touch `internal/traceability` (registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) — that belongs to the final leaf g0pcnt. Any edit there is a finding. Package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix are the right places.\\n\\n(8) **Mutation and hygiene.** Rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, and plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on gates the producer did not mutate, plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control. Per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators; NOT_APPLIED is not a pass. `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR tree or your copies. gofmt/vet clean. The candidate must be byte-identical to trunk everywhere outside this leaf's scope — check every path in `git diff --name-only <the CR base> <current origin/main>` that also appears in the candidate, because a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies that read as reverts. Crash and idempotency evidence is required for every durable write (a runtime directory and a server socket are durable writes) or an explicit purity bound. The full configured suite must be green on the exact tree; read the command count from the candidate config rather than assuming a number.\\n\\nReport the coverage ratio YOU measured against the acceptance table's real row count, not the producer's restated one. Attach TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev5.md and TASK-260830-35urbp_review-evidence-rev5.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then `accept_cr(TASK-260830-35urbp, revision=5, evidence=TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev5.md)` or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named and a short \\\"Rework scope (for the producer)\\\" section at the end. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 19070,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4768,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
