{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c45f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4fd-996a-7423-ba27-e5daf29de5a2"},"sequence":138,"recorded_at":1780531400000271,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c4fe-eaf8-7a33-a8ed-f5dcda7cc28c"},"task_id":"01a0c4fe-eaf8-7a33-a8ed-f5dcda7cc28c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c4fe-eaf8-7a33-a8ed-f5dcda7cc28c","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/acquire.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\n6|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// Caller names the acquisition caller. The vocabulary is owned by\n12|// internal/axpane, which already gates the wrapper decision over it;\n13|// this package reuses its constants rather than retyping them.\n14|type Caller = string\n15|\n16|const (\n17|\t// CallerForeground is an interactive operator-side caller that\n18|\t// may create the dedicated server.\n19|\tCallerForeground = axpane.CallerForeground\n20|\t// CallerBackground is a background CLI, SSH RPC process,\n21|\t// daemon, or restore worker: it must never create a\n22|\t// credential-dependent tmux server, may contact an\n23|\t// already-running authenticated broker, and otherwise receives\n24|\t// capability_unavailable with no fallback to direct creation.\n25|\tCallerBackground = axpane.CallerBackground\n26|)\n27|\n28|// Acquisition outcomes name how the caller reached the dedicated\n29|// server. Exactly one applies; there is no combined or fallback\n30|// outcome.\n31|const (\n32|\t// ViaSpawned created the dedicated -S server on the foreground\n33|\t// path and returns its spawn argv.\n34|\tViaSpawned = \"spawned\"\n35|\t// ViaAttachedFound the dedicated server already running and\n36|\t// attested on the foreground path.\n37|\tViaAttached = \"attached-running\"\n38|\t// ViaBroker contacted the already-running authenticated Aqua\n39|\t// broker and its attested AX tmux server on the background\n40|\t// path. No local spawn argv exists on this path.\n41|\tViaBroker = \"broker\"\n42|)\n43|\n44|// realmCapability is the Section 4.D capability the background\n45|// typed refusal names: the exact instance passes the AX sentinel\n46|// and the provider-auth smoke without UI. The admission verdict is\n47|// the landed terminalbackend owner's; this package consumes it\n48|// through RealmAdmission and never re-decides it.\n49|const realmCapability = \"credential_capable_execution_realm\"\n50|\n51|// ServerReport is the live dedicated-server probe result: whether\n52|// the private socket answers, with the landed admission verdict over\n53|// the exact server when it does.\n54|type ServerReport struct {\n55|\tRunning   bool\n56|\tAdmission RealmAdmission\n57|}\n58|\n59|// Dependencies carries every external interaction acquisition\n60|// performs. This leaf ships the decision core and argv only: no\n61|// production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree. The\n62|// exec/probe adapters — which report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence\n63|// verdicts and spawn through the built argv — and the server socket's\n64|// crash evidence are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz;\n65|// tests wire fakes. No probe runs without its dependency: a nil entry\n66|// refuses instead of reaching for a default.\n67|type Dependencies struct {\n68|\t// ProbeServer reports the dedicated socket's live state.\n69|\tProbeServer func(socket string) (ServerReport, error)\n70|\t// ProbeBroker reports the live Aqua broker state.\n71|\tProbeBroker func() (BrokerReport, error)\n72|\t// Spawn creates the dedicated server with the given -S argv.\n73|\tSpawn func(socket string, argv []string) error\n74|}\n75|\n76|// Request is the complete acquisition surface. There is deliberately\n77|// no member for a credential flag, a managername hint, or a cached\n78|// observation: the background creation rule needs no credential flag\n79|// because the background path never creates on any platform, and a\n80|// hint or cached observation never authorizes, so none is an input.\n81|type Request struct {\n82|\tCaller   Caller\n83|\tPlatform scalar.Platform\n84|\t// Root is the Runtime IPC root of the SPEC 3.2 table (macOS:\n85|\t// per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2:\n86|\t// $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax), resolved by the landed localstore\n87|\t// layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller — this leaf\n88|\t// resolves no root of its own, because the socket is runtime\n89|\t// IPC, never durable identity. The runtime leaf is not a\n90|\t// caller input: Acquire always passes RuntimeDirName, so the\n91|\t// derived socket is always <Root>/tmux/ax.sock and no caller\n92|\t// spelling can re-open the ambient or conventional names the\n93|\t// override gate refuses. Foreground acquisition ensures the\n94|\t// directory idempotently; background acquisition verifies the\n95|\t// existing directory and never creates it.\n96|\tRoot string\n97|\t// Ambient carries the observed ambient socket facts for\n98|\t// evidence. Resolution never reads them; tests assert the\n99|\t// acquired socket equals none of them.\n100|\tAmbient Ambient\n101|\t// SocketOverride must be empty. Any caller-supplied socket —\n102|\t// whichever ambient vector supplied it — refuses.\n103|\tSocketOverride string\n104|\t// SessionID is the logical session the spawned server will\n105|\t// host, as canonical UUIDv7. It shapes spawn argv only.\n106|\tSessionID string\n107|\t// Generation, BrokerState, and Remediation are the typed\n108|\t// realm/readiness details the capability_unavailable refusal\n109|\t// carries. All three are required: an input that omits one\n110|\t// is malformed and refuses invalid_arguments instead of\n111|\t// emitting an untyped refusal. Generation is also the typed\n112|\t// generation every admission must bind to.\n113|\tGeneration  string\n114|\tBrokerState string\n115|\tRemediation string\n116|\tDeps        Dependencies\n117|}\n118|\n119|// Outcome is the one acquisition result.\n120|type Outcome struct {\n121|\tVia    string\n122|\tSocket string\n123|\t// Argv is the dedicated -S spawn argv. It is set only for\n124|\t// ViaSpawned: the broker path spawns nothing and the\n125|\t// attached path presents through sibling-owned attach\n126|\t// semantics, not through a second spawn vector.\n127|\tArgv []string\n128|}\n129|\n130|// Acquire resolves the dedicated server socket from the runtime\n131|// directory and reaches the server through the caller-appropriate\n132|// path. Foreground attaches to the running attested server or\n133|// spawns the dedicated -S server; background contacts the\n134|// already-running authenticated broker or receives the typed\n135|// capability_unavailable refusal, and never falls back to direct\n136|// server creation — there is no spawn call on the background path,\n137|// and every background-path Acquire test arms a spy spawner that\n138|// fails the run if it is ever invoked.\n139|//\n140|// Refusals precede side effects: malformed input, ambient reuse, and\n141|// missing dependencies all refuse before any directory is created,\n142|// and background acquisition verifies the runtime directory without\n143|// creating it, so a background caller performs no durable write.\n144|func Acquire(req Request) (Outcome, error) {\n145|\tif req.Caller != CallerForeground && req.Caller != CallerBackground {\n146|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"caller\"}\n147|\t}\n148|\tif req.Generation == \"\" || req.BrokerState == \"\" || req.Remediation == \"\" {\n149|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"realm details\"}\n150|\t}\n151|\tdir, err := lexicalRuntimePath(req.Root, RuntimeDirName, req.Platform)\n152|\tif err != nil {\n153|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n154|\t}\n155|\tsocket, err := ResolveSocket(dir, req.SocketOverride, req.Ambient)\n156|\tif err != nil {\n157|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n158|\t}\n159|\tif req.Caller == CallerBackground {\n160|\t\treturn acquireBackground(req, socket)\n161|\t}\n162|\treturn acquireForeground(req, socket)\n163|}\n164|\n165|// acquireBackground implements the broker-or-refuse rule: it may\n166|// contact the already-running authenticated broker and its attested\n167|// server, and when neither exists it returns capability_unavailable\n168|// with typed realm/readiness details. Direct server creation is not\n169|// the else branch — this function has no path to the spawner, on\n170|// any platform — and the runtime directory is verified, never\n171|// created here. A missing leaf is the ordinary cold state (the\n172|// Runtime IPC root is a per-user temporary directory), so absence\n173|// maps to the typed unavailable with no broker probe and no spawn;\n174|// a leaf that exists but fails custody keeps its custody code.\n175|func acquireBackground(req Request, socket string) (Outcome, error) {\n176|\tif req.Deps.ProbeBroker == nil {\n177|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"dependencies\"}\n178|\t}\n179|\tverr := VerifyRuntimeDir(req.Root, RuntimeDirName, req.Platform)\n180|\tif runtimeAbsent(verr) {\n181|\t\treturn Outcome{}, backgroundUnavailable(req, verr)\n182|\t}\n183|\tif verr != nil {\n184|\t\treturn Outcome{}, verr\n185|\t}\n186|\tstatus, err := req.Deps.ProbeBroker()\n187|\tif err != nil {\n188|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n189|\t}\n190|\tif err := CheckBrokerContact(status, req.Generation, currentUID()); err != nil {\n191|\t\t// The miss path creates nothing: it consults the creation\n192|\t\t// gate so the no-fallback rule is enforced by a call, not\n193|\t\t// by the absence of one. The gate refuses every background\n194|\t\t// caller; its refusal is expected here and the path reports\n195|\t\t// the typed unavailable the spec names. The else branch is\n196|\t\t// reachable only when the gate is weakened to admit a\n197|\t\t// background caller, and then it refuses with the creation\n198|\t\t// code instead of the typed unavailable, so the committed\n199|\t\t// background-miss tests redden.\n200|\t\tif cerr := checkCreationAllowed(req.Caller); cerr != nil {\n201|\t\t\treturn Outcome{}, backgroundUnavailable(req, err)\n202|\t\t}\n203|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeBackgroundCreationRefused, Detail: \"background fallback\"}\n204|\t}\n205|\treturn Outcome{Via: ViaBroker, Socket: socket}, nil\n206|}\n207|\n208|// acquireForeground attaches to the running attested dedicated\n209|// server or spawns it. A running but unattested server refuses:\n210|// acquisition never attaches to a server whose landed admission is\n211|// missing or bound to another generation, and never repairs it here\n212|// — lifecycle owns that decision.\n213|func acquireForeground(req Request, socket string) (Outcome, error) {\n214|\tif req.Deps.ProbeServer == nil || req.Deps.Spawn == nil {\n215|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"dependencies\"}\n216|\t}\n217|\tensured, err := EnsureRuntimeDir(req.Root, RuntimeDirName, req.Platform, nil)\n218|\tif err != nil {\n219|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n220|\t}\n221|\treport, err := req.Deps.ProbeServer(socket)\n222|\tif err != nil {\n223|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n224|\t}\n225|\tif report.Running {\n226|\t\tif err := CheckServerAttested(report.Admission, req.Generation); err != nil {\n227|\t\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n228|\t\t}\n229|\t\treturn Outcome{Via: ViaAttached, Socket: socket}, nil\n230|\t}\n231|\targv, err := BuildArgv(ensured, socket, req.SessionID)\n232|\tif err != nil {\n233|\t\treturn Outcome{}, err\n234|\t}\n235|\tif err := req.Deps.Spawn(socket, argv); err != nil {\n236|\t\treturn Outcome{}, &Error{Code: CodeSpawnFailed, Detail: \"server spawn\"}\n237|\t}\n238|\treturn Outcome{Via: ViaSpawned, Socket: socket, Argv: argv}, nil\n239|}\n240|\n241|// runtimeAbsent reports whether err is the verify-side absent-leaf\n242|// refusal. Only the missing leaf counts — never a missing root, a\n243|// mode, ownership, kind, or symlink refusal: absence is the\n244|// readiness fact the background path maps to\n245|// capability_unavailable, while every unsafe-leaf refusal keeps its\n246|// custody code. A nil error is not absence.\n247|func runtimeAbsent(err error) bool {\n248|\tvar local *Error\n249|\tif !errors.As(err, &local) {\n250|\t\treturn false\n251|\t}\n252|\treturn local.Code == CodeUnsafeRuntimeDir && local.Detail == \"runtime absent\"\n253|}\n254|\n255|// checkCreationAllowed is the single choke point before every\n256|// direct server creation. A background caller never creates: on\n257|// macOS because server creation is credential-sensitive, and on\n258|// every platform because the background path must not fall back to\n259|// direct creation. The macOS credential-dependent case is one\n260|// fixture of this gate, not a narrower arm: narrowing the gate to\n261|// macOS or to credential-dependent servers would admit background\n262|// creation the no-fallback rule forbids. Foreground creation is\n263|// allowed on every platform; the credential binding it needs is\n264|// proven by the landed admission the server must present before\n265|// any attach.\n266|func checkCreationAllowed(caller Caller) error {\n267|\tif caller == CallerBackground {\n268|\t\treturn &Error{Code: CodeBackgroundCreationRefused, Detail: \"background creation\"}\n269|\t}\n270|\treturn nil\n271|}\n272|\n273|// backgroundUnavailable composes the typed capability_unavailable\n274|// refusal the spec names for the background miss, with the exact\n275|// Section 15.3 detail set. The constructor enforces the typed\n276|// details; a failure to render them is itself malformed input, not\n277|// an untyped refusal.\n278|func backgroundUnavailable(req Request, cause error) error {\n279|\tdetails := axerror.RealmEvidence{\n280|\t\tCapability:           realmCapability,\n281|\t\tCallerRealm:          req.Caller,\n282|\t\tBrokerState:          req.BrokerState,\n283|\t\tTmuxServerGeneration: req.Generation,\n284|\t\tRemediation:          req.Remediation,\n285|\t}\n286|\tfailure, err := axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable(axerror.Version130,\n287|\t\t\"no authenticated broker or attested tmux server\",\n288|\t\taxerror.NoIDs(), details, cause)\n289|\tif err != nil {\n290|\t\treturn &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"realm details\"}\n291|\t}\n292|\treturn failure\n293|}","final_result":true}}}
