{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c463","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4fd-996a-7423-ba27-e5daf29de5a2"},"sequence":140,"recorded_at":1780531400000275,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95"},"call_id":"call_01a0c4fee65075eebeb366eed635b7e1","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/acquire.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\n6|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// Caller names the acquisition caller. The vocabulary is owned by\n12|// internal/axpane, which already gates the wrapper decision over it;\n13|// this package reuses its constants rather than retyping them.\n14|type Caller = string\n15|\n16|const (\n17|\t// CallerForeground is an interactive operator-side caller that\n18|\t// may create the dedicated server.\n19|\tCallerForeground = axpane.CallerForeground\n20|\t// CallerBackground is a background CLI, SSH RPC process,\n21|\t// daemon, or restore worker: it must never create a\n22|\t// credential-dependent tmux server, may contact an\n23|\t// already-running authenticated broker, and otherwise receives\n24|\t// capability_unavailable with no fallback to direct creation.\n25|\tCallerBackground = axpane.CallerBackground\n26|)\n27|\n28|// Acquisition outcomes name how the caller reached the dedicated\n29|// server. Exactly one applies; there is no combined or fallback\n30|// outcome.\n31|const (\n32|\t// ViaSpawned created the dedicated -S server on the foreground\n33|\t// path and returns its spawn argv.\n34|\tViaSpawned = \"spawned\"\n35|\t// ViaAttachedFound the dedicated server already running and\n36|\t// attested on the foreground path.\n37|\tViaAttached = \"attached-running\"\n38|\t// ViaBroker contacted the already-running authenticated Aqua\n39|\t// broker and its attested AX tmux server on the background\n40|\t// path. No local spawn argv exists on this path.\n41|\tViaBroker = \"broker\"\n42|)\n43|\n44|// realmCapability is the Section 4.D capability the background\n45|// typed refusal names: the exact instance passes the AX sentinel\n46|// and the provider-auth smoke without UI. The admission verdict is\n47|// the landed terminalbackend owner's; this package consumes it\n48|// through RealmAdmission and never re-decides it.\n49|const realmCapability = \"credential_capable_execution_realm\"\n50|\n51|// ServerReport is the live dedicated-server probe result: whether\n52|// the private socket answers, with the landed admission verdict over\n53|// the exact server when it does.\n54|type ServerReport struct {\n55|\tRunning   bool\n56|\tAdmission RealmAdmission\n57|}\n58|\n59|// Dependencies carries every external interaction acquisition\n60|// performs. This leaf ships the decision core and argv only: no\n61|// production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree. The\n62|// exec/probe adapters — which report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence\n63|// verdicts and spawn through the built argv — and the server socket's\n64|// crash evidence are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz;\n65|// tests wire fakes. No probe runs without its dependency: a nil entry\n66|// refuses instead of reaching for a default.\n67|type Dependencies struct {\n68|\t// ProbeServer reports the dedicated socket's live state.\n69|\tProbeServer func(socket string) (ServerReport, error)\n70|\t// ProbeBroker reports the live Aqua broker state.\n71|\tProbeBroker func() (BrokerReport, error)\n72|\t// Spawn creates the dedicated server with the given -S argv.\n73|\tSpawn func(socket string, argv []string) error\n74|}\n75|\n76|// Request is the complete acquisition surface. There is deliberately\n77|// no member for a credential flag, a managername hint, or a cached\n78|// observation: the background creation rule needs no credential flag\n79|// because the background path never creates on any platform, and a\n80|// hint or cached observation never authorizes, so none is an input.\n81|type Request struct {\n82|\tCaller   Caller\n83|\tPlatform scalar.Platform\n84|\t// Root is the Runtime IPC root of the SPEC 3.2 table (macOS:\n85|\t// per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2:\n86|\t// $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax), resolved by the landed localstore\n87|\t// layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller — this leaf\n88|\t// resolves no root of its own, because the socket is runtime\n89|\t// IPC, never durable identity. The runtime leaf is not a\n90|\t// caller input: Acquire always passes RuntimeDirName, so the\n91|\t// derived socket is always <Root>/tmux/ax.sock and no caller\n92|\t// spelling can re-open the ambient or conventional names the\n93|\t// override gate refuses. Foreground acquisition ensures the\n94|\t// directory idempotently; background acquisition verifies the\n95|\t// existing directory and never creates it.\n96|\tRoot string\n97|\t// Ambient carries the observed ambient socket facts for\n98|\t// evidence. Resolution never reads them; tests assert the\n99|\t// acquired socket equals none of them.\n100|\tAmbient Ambient\n101|\t// SocketOverride must be empty. Any caller-supplied socket —\n102|\t// whichever ambient vector supplied it — refuses.\n103|\tSocketOverride string\n104|\t// SessionID is the logical session the spawned server will\n105|\t// host, as canonical UUIDv7. It shapes spawn argv only.\n106|\tSessionID string\n107|\t// Generation, BrokerState, and Remediation are the typed\n108|\t// realm/readiness details the capability_unavailable refusal\n109|\t// carries. All three are required: an input that omits one\n110|\t// is malformed and refuses invalid_arguments instead of