{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c655","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4fd-996a-7423-ba27-e5daf29de5a2"},"sequence":389,"recorded_at":1780531400000773,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c509-0a4b-7a83-b2b6-6904dee3475b"},"task_id":"01a0c509-0a4b-7a83-b2b6-6904dee3475b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c509-0a4b-7a83-b2b6-6904dee3475b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-7-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat \\\"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md\\\" 2>&1 | head -150\",\n  \"description\": \"Read current results head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# TASK-260830-35urbp results — implement-private-tmux-server-management (rev5)\\n\\nRework of revision 4 after review-verdict-rev4 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no\\nP1, two P2 classes, two P3). First leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i\\n(production-tmux-backend, EPIC M1). The reviewer states every rev3\\nfinding (P2-A/B/C, P3-A..E, the four observations) is closed with\\ndriven evidence and stays closed, and that production behaves\\ncorrectly at every point the review drove; this revision keeps all of\\nthat and changes only what the verdict grades open.\\n\\nCandidate: UNCOMMITTED working tree on branch\\n`task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i` atop trunk `799c338` (trunk\\nunmoved since rev4; no refresh, no rebase, no commit, no merge by this\\nrun). `git status` shows only `internal/tmuxserver/`, `README.md`,\\n`LOGBOOK.md`.\\n\\nNormative source: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\\n§3.2 platform paths (lines 765-813: the dedicated socket\\n`<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root) and §4.2 tmux\\nbackend (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220), and\\n§4.E (1309) as context, plus §4.3 (1458) and §4.4 for the Windows\\nand broker rules. All clause citations name the pinned file, never\\nthe network, never v0.5.0.\\n\\n## Finding-by-finding table (verdict -> change -> test that fails without it -> evidence)\\n\\n| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| P2-A custody oracle looks through the wrapper; no narrowing admits a member the absence classifier must reject | `requireLocalError` now asserts the TOP-LEVEL `*Error` dynamic type plus no reachable `*axerror.Error` (the wrapper IS the observable refusal: the cause is redacted off the wire). Shipped `N-absence-remap-widen` in the reviewer's R05 shape (`runtimeAbsent` admitting `runtime mode`); kept `N-background-absence-remap` (rewritten to the platform conjunct after the `Request.Name` deletion) for the reject direction. Re-ran every custody row after the oracle change: none only passed because of the old helper | `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal` (a widened 0755 leaf maps to `capability_unavailable` under the mutant; the top-level assertion reddens). Proven load-bearing: the row SURVIVES under the old helper (reproduces R05) and KILLS under the fixed one | `harness-pass1/N-absence-remap-widen.log`, `harness-pass1/N-background-absence-remap.log` (+ pass 2), `plant-replays/N-absence-remap-widen.log` + `oracle-replay-old-verdict.log` (old-oracle SURVIVED replay) |\\n| P2-B `Request.Name` re-opens the §3.2 divergence per call; the spec path pinned at the constants, not the entry | `Request.Name` DELETED: `Acquire` always passes `RuntimeDirName`, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths. `EnsureRuntimeDir`/`VerifyRuntimeDir` keep their `name` parameter for the grammar rows. New `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` through `Acquire` for foreground and background; rows 16/56 name it. The P01 probe is unstageable (the field does not exist) and R11 inapplicable | `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` (foreground, background subtests; any caller-selectable leaf or renamed constant reddens) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `internal/tmuxserver/acquire.go` |\\n| P3-A absence remap pinned on the macOS axis only | `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` now drives macos, linux, and wsl2 subtests (the cold state is identical: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is tmpfs); named under row 52 | The linux/wsl2 subtests (the reviewer's R14 shape fails on both firsthand, macos still maps) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `R14-replay.log` (R14 plant: macos PASS, linux/wsl2 FAIL) |\\n| P3-B censusable \\\"every background test arms a spy\\\" is false (7 of 11) | Armed the spy in all four (`TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid`, `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf`, the background half of `TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies`, the background iteration of `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform`, each asserting zero calls) and scoped the README/`acquire.go` sentence to background-path `Acquire` tests. Mechanical census: 12/12 armed (incl. the new background subtest) | The four tests' new zero-call assertions (a guarded `D-background-fallback`-shaped plant is visible to all of them) | `pkg-tests-v.log` |\\n| Obs R03/ELOOP, unopenable root, Fchmod/Fsync/Stat arms, nested invocation, vacuous members | One-sentence TRACEABILITY entries: ELOOP darwin-equivalence under row 6 (reasoned, not run); the 0000-root arm and the `Fchmod`/`Fsync`/leaf-`Stat` arms under B15 as error-arm rows; the nested-invocation over-strict refusal under B16 (owner TASK-260830-1c28dz); the live-member scoping (`TMUXEnv`/`InheritedSocket` only) under row 23; the `localstore`-root caller contract stated as undriven under B19 | — (bounds/prose, no behavior) | `TRACEABILITY.md` rows 6/23, B15/B16/B19 |\\n\\nKept untouched per the verdict: the dedicated-server rule per vector,\\nthe background broker-or-refuse wiring with the literal\\n`capability_unavailable` and typed details, the no-fallback rule along\\nthe caller/credential/platform axes, the landed-admission attestation\\ncomposition (incl. the admission-empty Running pins), the custody\\ngates that held under attack (FIFO/symlink/mode/UID/handle-mismatch\\nrefusals, the explicit `Fchmod`, the real-SIGKILL crash test), the\\ndeterminism design (no real-tmux witness), and the\\n`internal/traceability` boundary.\\n\\n## Deliverable (rev5 shape)\\n\\n`internal/tmuxserver`, composing the landed owners (never forked):\\n\\n- (1) Runtime custody: `EnsureRuntimeDir` / `VerifyRuntimeDir` with\\n  three independent gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership).\\n  Foreground acquisition ensures idempotently; background acquisition\\n  verifies the existing directory and never creates it. Absence\\n  (`ENOENT`) carries its own detail; the missing-root mapping is one\\n  shared classifier.\\n- (2) Dedicated socket: `SocketPath` / `ResolveSocket` derive\\n  `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` — the spec's path — and refuse overrides and\\n  ambient collisions on all five members, with the TMUX member\\n  compared in its real encoding and unclean spellings cleaned\\n  (symlink aliases bound). The runtime leaf is not an `Acquire`\\n  input: the entry always passes `RuntimeDirName`.\\n- (3) Acquisition: `Acquire` refuses malformed input, ambient reuse,\\n  and missing dependencies before any side effect. Foreground attaches\\n  or spawns (a running server never spawns, even with empty\\n  admission); background brokers-or-refuses with the typed\\n  `capability_unavailable` — including the absent-leaf cold state on\\n  macOS, Linux, and WSL2 — and no fallback (the miss path consults\\n  the creation gate by call; every background-path `Acquire` test arms\\n  a zero-call spy).\\n- (4) Readiness: `CheckServerAttested` / `CheckBrokerContact` decide\\n  the landed admission (`Admitted.Has(realm)` + generation equality)\\n  over a typed same-user generation-bound broker principal. A stale\\n  admission — the replayed-cached shape — refuses on both paths.\\n- (5) Spawn argv: `BuildArgv` emits exactly\\n  `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session`\\n  through the landed argv gate. Native Windows refuses every request.\\n\\nExtended vs deliberately not extended (unchanged from rev4; the\\nreviewer verified each claim rather than accepting it):\\n\\n- Extended (composed): `terminalbackend.Admitted` (attestation\\n  verdict), `axpane` caller vocabulary, `axerror` typed refusal,\\n  `scalar` platform/path/UUIDv7 grammars, `secprim` Guard /\\n  `OpenNoFollowDir` / `CheckArgv`, the `localstore` Runtime IPC root\\n  (`PathRuntime`, consumed as the caller-supplied `Request.Root` —\\n  this leaf resolves no root of its own), the `hosttrust`\\n  verify-never-repair precedent, the `termbind` crash-hook pattern.\\n- Deliberately not extended: `hosttrust` custody itself (Host Channel\\n  authority — a tmux runtime dir is not a trust store);\\n  `terminalbackend` Reconcile evidence admission (consumed, not\\n  re-owned); `axpane` checkRealm (unexported; this leaf composes the\\n  same Has-plus-generation-equality over the probe-reported verdict);\\n  the host-binding/provider-build cross-bind (stays with the lifecycle\\n  owner, bound B13); `terminstance` lifecycle execution (sibling leaf);\\n  `secprim`'s private `guardRootMatches` (mirrored as\\n  `handleBoundToPath` with a seam because the original is unexported);\\n  `internal/traceability` (untouched — bindings and the re-pin belong\\n  to the final leaf).\\n\\nDeterminism: every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs\\nthrough injected dependencies. No test starts a tmux process; the\\nsuite passes with the tmux binary unresolvable and no tmux process on\\nthe host (71 top-level PASS, 0 SKIP in the tmux-hidden run). No AC row\\nhas a real-tmux witness — that is the design, not a gap (bound B1).\\n\\n## Coverage ratio (measured, not planned)\\n\\n**58 of 58 AC rows driven** through production entries by named\\ncommitted tests — matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`,\\nreproduced with spec-clause mapping in\\n`TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md` (rev5). Rows 16/56 name the\\nnew entry-level spec-path test on both callers, row 52 names the\\nmacos/linux/wsl2 absence subtests and the top-level custody oracle,\\nrow 6 states the ELOOP equivalence, row 23 scopes the live collision\\nmembers, and the mutant-to-gate map names all 55 narrowing rows.\\n\\n## Mutants (shipped harness, per-plant raw logs)\\n\\n`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py` —\\n55 narrowing + 1 supplementary additive (D-background-fallback,\\nlabeled) + 1 harmless SURVIVED control. Pass 1 and pass 2: **57/57\\neach, verdict lists identical**, exit 0. Per-row raw logs (go output +\\nsubprocess exit) for both passes are in the evidence tarball;\\nproduction blobs byte-identical before/after every run\\n(`git status` shows only candidate paths). No token-preserving\\nsource-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text (stated\\nbound B4, harness executes the behavioral suite). The one\\nnil-dependency narrowing that kills by panic (N-deps-foreground) is\\ndisclosed in the harness and the matrix; N-deps-background kills by\\nan unavailable-vs-dependencies mismatch since the admitted request\\nreaches Verify on the absent leaf. N-fchmod-umask and the\\nread-only-root test assume a non-root test user (bound B14), the same\\nshape as the reviewer's plant. N-broker-empty-generation,\\nN-commit-eacces-as-exist, and the background leg of\\nN-verify-absence-detail kill by reroute to a neighboring refusal,\\ndisclosed in their row notes. The reviewers' error-arm plants\\n(stat-failure arms flipped to fail-open, the unreachable guard arm,\\nthe unopenable-root arm) are reported as error-arm rows under bound\\nB15 and are never counted among the narrowing survivors.\\n\\n## Crash / idempotency (unchanged from rev4)\\n\\nReal SIGKILL seam (unix): `TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates`\\n(child runs the genuine `EnsureRuntimeDir` entry and kills itself in\\n`AfterMkdir`, after mkdirat and before verification plus parent\\nfsync; parent proves the retry converges to the one verified\\ndirectory). Idempotent replay: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent`,\\n`TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently`,\\n`TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry` (spawn-then-retry\\nattaches with exactly one spawn). Crash convergence states the umask\\nbound B10; the server socket's crash evidence is owned by the\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 11371,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2843,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
