lback rule along\\nthe caller/credential/platform axes, the landed-admission attestation\\ncomposition (incl. the admission-empty Running pins), the custody\\ngates that held under attack (FIFO/symlink/mode/UID/handle-mismatch\\nrefusals, the explicit `Fchmod`, the real-SIGKILL crash test), the\\ndeterminism design (no real-tmux witness), and the\\n`internal/traceability` boundary.\\n\\n## Deliverable (rev5 shape)\\n\\n`internal/tmuxserver`, composing the landed owners (never forked):\\n\\n- (1) Runtime custody: `EnsureRuntimeDir` / `VerifyRuntimeDir` with\\n  three independent gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership).\\n  Foreground acquisition ensures idempotently; background acquisition\\n  verifies the existing directory and never creates it. Absence\\n  (`ENOENT`) carries its own detail; the missing-root mapping is one\\n  shared classifier.\\n- (2) Dedicated socket: `SocketPath` / `ResolveSocket` derive\\n  `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` — the spec's path — and refuse overrides and\\n  ambient collisions on all five members, with the TMUX member\\n  compared in its real encoding and unclean spellings cleaned\\n  (symlink aliases bound). The runtime leaf is not an `Acquire`\\n  input: the entry always passes `RuntimeDirName`.\\n- (3) Acquisition: `Acquire` refuses malformed input, ambient reuse,\\n  and missing dependencies before any side effect. Foreground attaches\\n  or spawns (a running server never spawns, even with empty\\n  admission); background brokers-or-refuses with the typed\\n  `capability_unavailable` — including the absent-leaf cold state on\\n  macOS, Linux, and WSL2 — and no fallback (the miss path consults\\n  the creation gate by call; every background-path `Acquire` test arms\\n  a zero-call spy).\\n- (4) Readiness: `CheckServerAttested` / `CheckBrokerContact` decide\\n  the landed admission (`Admitted.Has(realm)` + generation equality)\\n  over a typed same-user generation-bound broker principal. A stale\\n  admission — the replayed-cached