{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c751","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4fd-996a-7423-ba27-e5daf29de5a2"},"sequence":515,"recorded_at":1780531400001025,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95"},"call_id":"call_01a0c50dc46e75a4b1e52ca5d53ba7e4","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/doc.go`.\n1|// Package tmuxserver owns AX private tmux server management: owner-only\n2|// runtime directories and dedicated tmux -S servers with no ambient or\n3|// default-server discovery or reuse. It is the first leaf of the\n4|// production-tmux-backend story.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 3.2 (platform paths: the\n7|// dedicated socket `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC\n8|// root — the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity) and\n9|// Section 4.2 (tmux backend, dedicated -S server,\n10|// credential-sensitive creation, background broker-or-refuse,\n11|// launchctl managername as diagnostic hint only, cached observations\n12|// never authorize resume), Section 4.C (operation vocabulary cited for\n13|// the wrapper entrypoint shape only), Section 4.D (capability evidence\n14|// cited landed), and Section 4.E (sensitive runtime state is owner-only\n15|// and non-replicable).\n16|//\n17|// Division of authority (composed, never forked): the caller vocabulary\n18|// (foreground/background) comes from internal/axpane, which already\n19|// gates the wrapper decision over it; the capability_unavailable typed\n20|// refusal comes from internal/axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable, which\n21|// enforces the exact Section 15.3 detail set; the attestation verdict\n22|// comes from the landed internal/terminalbackend admission\n23|// (Reconcile/ResolveEvidence), consumed here as an Admitted set\n24|// composed only with the generation equality the wrapper owner\n25|// already enforces — sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n26|// verification, liveness, and expiry are the admission's verdict, not\n27|// this leaf's; path grammars come from internal/scalar (absolute root,\n28|// relative member, UUIDv7 session); the Runtime IPC root value comes\n29|// from the landed internal/localstore layout (PathRuntime), resolved\n30|// by the caller and supplied as Request.Root — this leaf resolves no\n31|// root of its own; lexical containment comes from\n32|// internal/secprim.Guard; argv shape validation comes from\n33|// internal/secprim.CheckArgv. What this package owns is the composition\n34|// no landed package provides: the descriptor-relative runtime-directory\n35|// commit (mkdirat from a pinned root handle, not a path-string\n36|// MkdirAll), the three independent custody gates (mode, ownership,\n37|// containment), the five-member ambient non-use proof (TMUX and\n38|// TMUX_TMPDIR environment values, inherited socket, default path,\n39|// conventional name), the background broker-or-refuse acquisition path\n40|// with its no-fallback gate over a typed same-user generation-bound\n41|// broker principal, the foreground ensure-then-attach-or-spawn path,\n42|// and the dedicated -S argv builder.\n43|//\n44|// Bounds: no ax CLI surface, no lifecycle operations (create, attach,\n45|// status, quiesce, stop, terminate, restore belong to the sibling\n46|// leaves), no ConPTY process control, no provider process, no mesh\n47|// transport, and no production probe or spawner implementation —\n48|// caller-supplied probes report the landed admission verdicts, and the\n49|// exec/probe adapters are sibling scope. Native Windows refuses every\n50|// request. No test in this package starts a tmux process: every\n51|// broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through injected\n52|// dependencies, and the suite passes with no tmux installed.\n53|package tmuxserver","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
