{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7f7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4fd-996a-7423-ba27-e5daf29de5a2"},"sequence":598,"recorded_at":1780531400001191,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e01e1bc2-95c9-4151-a1a6-6ebbbbe18d95"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c50e-58ca-7762-8c91-16fefdf0d37e"},"task_id":"01a0c50e-58ca-7762-8c91-16fefdf0d37e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c50e-58ca-7762-8c91-16fefdf0d37e","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2328 line(s) above)\n2329|## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\n2330|\n2331|[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\n2332|directories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or\n2333|default-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 3.2, 4.2, 4.C-4.E).\n2334|The dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC\n2335|root (per-user temporary directory on macOS, `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax` on\n2336|Linux/WSL2), resolved by the landed `localstore` layout and supplied by\n2337|the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity.\n2338|`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root\n2339|handle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three\n2340|independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\n2341|ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\n2342|verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\n2343|server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\n2344|override on all five ambient members (`TMUX` and `TMUX_TMPDIR`\n2345|environment values, inherited socket, default path, conventional\n2346|`default` name). `Acquire` reaches the server through the\n2347|caller-appropriate path: foreground ensures the directory, then attaches\n2348|to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S` server whose\n2349|stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while background\n2350|verifies the existing directory without creating it, contacts only the\n2351|already-running authenticated same-user broker and its attested server,\n2352|and a miss — including an absent runtime directory, the ordinary\n2353|post-reboot cold state — returns the typed `capability_unavailable`\n2354|refusal with realm/readiness details, while an existing-but-unsafe\n2355|directory keeps its custody refusal — there is no fallback to direct\n2356|creation, and every background-path `Acquire` test arms a spy spawner\n2357|that fails the run if it is ever invoked. Attestation is the landed `terminalbackend`\n2358|Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission consumed as an `Admitted` set\n2359|composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\n2360|stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\n2361|live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\n2362|runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\n2363|process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request.\n2364|\n2365|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n2366|\n2367|```bash\n2368|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\n2369|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\n2370|```\n2371|\n2372|Run the narrowing battery (55 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\n2373|additive row, plus one harmless control) with:\n2374|\n2375|```bash\n2376|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\n2377|```\n2378|\n2379|The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n2380|through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n2381|reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n2382|additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\n2383|raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n2384|attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\n2385|`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\n2386|matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n2387|[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2388|\n2389|## Ownership reducer properties\n2390|\n2391|The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\n2392|and 13.6-13.10) hold as executable property tests over the landed production\n2393|reducers — `sessstate.Reduce` with `Compare` and the union projection,\n2394|`sessrepo.WinningLease` with `ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`:\n2395|\n2396|1. Union-order independence: every permutation of a union multiset, and every\n2397|   partition into successive unions, projects byte-identically (winner,\n2398|   conflicts, divergent-history warnings). Losing-branch evidence is a pure\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
